  {"type": "split", "h2": "Why we're picky about the brands we carry", "image": "Midea cold-climate heat pump installed by EHI on a raised stand", "image_src": "/assets/img/work/midea-cold-climate-heat-pump-stand-1.webp", "image_fit": "cover", "image_pos": "50% 62%", "image_credit": "EHI install", "html": "<p>Plenty of HVAC contractors will install whatever the supplier has on the shelf that week. We carry four brands on purpose, and each one had to clear the same four tests before we put our name beside it.</p><p><strong>Parts you can get in Ontario.</strong> A heat pump is only as good as the part you need on a Sunday in January. We chose lines where we have dealer access to parts and technical support, so a repair is a day, not a month.</p><p><strong>Real cold-climate ratings.</strong> Midea EVOX G3 and Kepler are rated to heat at -30°C. That matters in Barrie, Sudbury and North Bay, and honestly it matters in Markham too during a cold snap.</p><p><strong>On the NRCan qualified products list.</strong> The Home Renovation Savings Program only pays out on heat pumps that make the list. We check the exact model and size before we quote, so your up to $7,500 rebate is real and not a hope. Confirm eligibility before installation, and remember program terms can change.</p><p><strong>Warranty support that works.</strong> Authorized dealers can register your warranty, access extended coverage of up to 12 years parts and labour on select systems, and get a manufacturer on the phone. A contractor buying grey-market equipment online cannot. See our <a href='/warranty/'>warranty page</a> for how coverage works.</p>"},
